# Fix: Date Hallucination & Email Fetching Crashes

After removing the demo data, the AI was forced to rely on its real tools. However, two underlying bugs were immediately exposed during testing:

## Root Cause Analysis

| # | User Symptom | Root Cause in Code |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | The AI searches for random past dates like `2023-10-25` when asked for "today" | [orchestrator.py](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/orchestrator.py) has a typo in the prompt template: `- Today's date is: {{ $today }}`. Python's `.format(today=...)` ignores it because of the double braces (`{{`). The AI receives the literal string `{{ $today }}` instead of the date, so it hallucinates a fake date. |
| 2 | "Failed to fetch emails: 400 Client Error" | [outlook_client.py](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py) inserts queries directly into the Graph API OData filter: `$filter=contains(subject, 'Lab 4 security')`. Microsoft Graph API crashes with a `400 Bad Request` when given multi-word exact matches in `contains()`. |

## Proposed Changes

### [Orchestrator](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/orchestrator.py)

#### [MODIFY] [orchestrator.py](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/orchestrator.py)
**Fix 1:** Change `{{ $today }}` to `{today}` on line 375 so the Python `.format()` call correctly injects the current date into the system prompt.

### [OutlookClient](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py)

#### [MODIFY] [outlook_client.py](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py)
**Fix 2:** Remove the `subject_contains` OData filter entirely. Move the filtering to the client-side loop using standard Python string matching (`q in email["subject"].lower()`), exactly as we do for `sender_contains`. This bypasses the Graph API limitation while retaining functionality.

## Verification Plan
1. Restart the bot (`python main.py`)
2. Ask "Any important emails today?" -> AI should now know today's real date and query it
3. Ask "Read the Lab 4 security email" -> The multi-word subject filter should work client-side without crashing the API
